---
title: "api e exception: a porta HTTP e os erros"
---
classDiagram
    direction TB
    class CitizenLife {
        <<final>>
        +main(String[] args)$ void
    }
    class HttpHandler {
        <<interface>>
        +handle(HttpExchange) void
    }
    class Servidor {
        +Servidor(CidadaoService, RotaService, EnderecoService, OcorrenciaService)
        +handle(HttpExchange) void
    }
    class Json {
        <<final>>
        +escrever(Object)$ String
        +ler(String)$ Object
    }
    class RuntimeException
    class CitizenLifeException {
        -int status
        +naoEncontrado(String)$ CitizenLifeException
        +naoAutenticado(String)$ CitizenLifeException
        +acessoNegado(String)$ CitizenLifeException
        +conflito(String, Throwable)$ CitizenLifeException
        +bancoIndisponivel(String, Throwable)$ CitizenLifeException
    }
    class ValidacaoException {
        -Map~String,String~ erros
        +texto(campo, valor, rotulo, min, max) String
        +exigir(boolean, campo, mensagem) void
        +erro(campo, mensagem) void
        +lancarSeHouverErros() void
    }
    CitizenLife ..> Servidor : cria
    HttpHandler <|.. Servidor
    Servidor ..> Json
    Servidor ..> CitizenLifeException : responde erro e campos
    RuntimeException <|-- CitizenLifeException
    CitizenLifeException <|-- ValidacaoException
